 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "Temporarily producing a protein from a gene introduced into cells, without the gene becoming a permanent part of the cell's genome.",
 "description": {
  "text": "The temporary expression of genes for a short time after nucleic acid, usually plasmid DNA, is introduced into eukaryotic cells with a chemical delivery agent. Unlike stable expression, the foreign DNA does not fuse into the cell's genome.",
